{
  "id": "arranging_coins",
  "title": "Arranging Coins",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Algorithms",
  "tags": [
    "Math",
    "Binary Search"
  ],
  "description": "<p>You have <code>n</code> coins and you want to build a staircase with these coins. The staircase consists of <code>k</code> rows where the <code>i<sup>th</sup></code> row has exactly <code>i</code> coins. The last row of the staircase <strong>may be</strong> incomplete.</p> <p>Given the integer <code>n</code>, return <em>the number of <strong>complete rows</strong> of the staircase you will build</em>.</p> <p> </p> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p> <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2021/04/09/arrangecoins1-grid.jpg\" style=\"width: 253px; height: 253px;\"/> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 5\n<strong>Output:</strong> 2\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> Because the 3<sup>rd</sup> row is incomplete, we return 2.\n</pre> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p> <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2021/04/09/arrangecoins2-grid.jpg\" style=\"width: 333px; height: 333px;\"/> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 8\n<strong>Output:</strong> 3\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> Because the 4<sup>th</sup> row is incomplete, we return 3.\n</pre> <p> </p> <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p> <ul> <li><code>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 2<sup>31</sup> - 1</code></li> </ul>",
  "hints": [],
